<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akrotiri (prehistoric city)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akrotiri is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> settlement on the island of Santorini (Thera) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, buried by a volcanic eruption in the 17th or 16th century BCE. Excavated since 1967, its well-preserved multi-storey houses and wall paintings make it one of the most important sites of the Aegean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> Age. Its inhabitants appear to have fled before the eruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akrotiri-prehistoric-city.jpg" alt="Akrotiri (prehistoric city)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rt44 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Akrotiri.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
